WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.571
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:09.304
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.604 --> 00:00:17.678
Unit twenty: Exam Day: Review and Time Management. Today you will plan your time and avoid common mistakes in the exam.

4
00:00:17.978 --> 00:00:20.444
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.459
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:26.225
Exam.

7
00:00:27.217 --> 00:00:29.332
Exam means a formal test.

8
00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:31.452
The exam starts at eight.

9
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.308
Your turn. Say: Exam.

10
00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.168
Exam.

11
00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:39.755
Revision.

12
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.516
Revision means studying again before a test.

13
00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:45.791
Do revision every day.

14
00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:48.827
Your turn. Say: Revision.

15
00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:52.912
Revision.

16
00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:54.744
Time limit.

17
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.226
Time limit means the fixed time for the task.

18
00:00:58.817 --> 00:01:00.189
Watch the time limit.

19
00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:03.436
Your turn. Say: Time limit.

20
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.266
Time limit.

21
00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:08.716
Plan.

22
00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:11.856
Plan means a set of steps to follow.

23
00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:13.556
Make a plan.

24
00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.338
Your turn. Say: Plan.

25
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.004
Plan.

26
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:21.426
Check.

27
00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:24.846
Check means to look again for mistakes.

28
00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:26.660
Check your answers.

29
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.786
Your turn. Say: Check.

30
00:01:32.633 --> 00:01:33.240
Check.

31
00:01:33.983 --> 00:01:34.694
Calm.

32
00:01:35.683 --> 00:01:36.998
Calm means relaxed.

33
00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:38.654
Stay calm.

34
00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.484
Your turn. Say: Calm.

35
00:01:44.333 --> 00:01:45.091
Calm.

36
00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:46.956
Instruction.

37
00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:50.600
Instruction means a rule that tells you what to do.

38
00:01:51.183 --> 00:01:52.742
Read every instruction.

39
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.968
Your turn. Say: Instruction.

40
00:01:58.833 --> 00:01:59.985
Instruction.

41
00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:01.635
Priority.

42
00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.800
Priority means something more important.

43
00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:07.416
Easy questions are a priority.

44
00:02:08.017 --> 00:02:10.599
Your turn. Say: Priority.

45
00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.481
Priority.

46
00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:18.871
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.717 --> 00:02:22.703
Visal, how should I prepare in the last week?

48
00:02:23.817 --> 00:02:32.913
Review the main grammar points, practise past exam papers and sleep well. Do not try to learn many new things the night before.

49
00:02:34.017 --> 00:02:36.074
How should I use time in the exam?

50
00:02:37.183 --> 00:02:46.825
Read all instructions, answer the easy questions first and keep a little time at the end. If a question is hard, move on and return later.

51
00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:49.347
How do I stay calm?

52
00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:58.396
Breathe slowly, drink some water and trust your preparation. Never leave a blank, because a guess may be correct.

53
00:02:59.533 --> 00:03:00.918
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.783 --> 00:03:05.675
Grammar focus: Strategy: plan, answer, check.

55
00:03:05.975 --> 00:03:07.174
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.883 --> 00:03:10.394
I read all the instructions before I start.

57
00:03:11.283 --> 00:03:14.130
I check my answers in the last five minutes.

58
00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:20.178
Read the instructions, answer easy questions first, never leave a blank and check your work at the end.

59
00:03:20.917 --> 00:03:24.730
Be careful! Don't say: I leave hard questions blank.

60
00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:29.235
Say: I guess if I do not know.

61
00:03:29.535 --> 00:03:31.001
Never leave blanks.

62
00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.441
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:35.233 --> 00:03:36.327
Exam Morning.

64
00:03:36.627 --> 00:03:39.881
Rina arrives at the exam hall early and stays calm.

65
00:03:40.867 --> 00:03:43.354
She reads all the instructions carefully.

66
00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:46.633
She answers the easy questions first.

67
00:03:47.633 --> 00:03:50.028
She moves on when a question is too hard.

68
00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:54.380
In the last five minutes she checks her answers.

69
00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:59.201
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:02.305
Before starting the exam you should blank.

71
00:04:02.605 --> 00:04:06.491
A, draw. B, sleep. C, read the instructions.

72
00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:12.706
The answer is C: read the instructions.

73
00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.838
Answer blank questions first.

74
00:04:16.138 --> 00:04:19.397
A, easy. B, hard. C, no.

75
00:04:22.933 --> 00:04:25.107
The answer is A: easy.

76
00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.319
If a question is hard, you should blank.

77
00:04:28.619 --> 00:04:32.644
A, cry. B, move on and return. C, stop.

78
00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.861
The answer is B: move on and return.

79
00:04:40.017 --> 00:04:41.424
Never leave a blank.

80
00:04:41.724 --> 00:04:44.785
A, pen. B, door. C, blank.

81
00:04:48.333 --> 00:04:50.310
The answer is C: blank.

82
00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:52.892
How does Rina feel?

83
00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:56.172
A, calm. B, angry. C, bored.

84
00:04:59.733 --> 00:05:01.280
The answer is A: calm.

85
00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:05.514
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:08.489
What is your plan for the exam day?

87
00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:18.772
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:19.072 --> 00:05:29.355
I will arrive early and read all the instructions. I will answer the easy questions first and keep time to check my answers. I will stay calm and never leave a blank.

89
00:05:29.655 --> 00:05:31.294
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:32.183 --> 00:05:37.587
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: plan, answer, check.

91
00:05:37.887 --> 00:05:42.873
Today's value is self-discipline. Control your habits, so your habits do not control you.

92
00:05:43.173 --> 00:05:50.484
Congratulations! You have finished Online Cambodia Grade nine English. See you in Online Grade twelve English!

93
00:05:50.784 --> 00:05:53.808
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

